<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="kicker">Editions</span>
      <h2>How CodeStorm grew</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid--3">
      <article class="card">
        <figure class="media">
          <img src="assets/img/past-3.svg" width="700" height="500" alt="CodeStorm 2023 launch edition artwork">
        </figure>
        <p style="margin-top:1rem"><span class="badge">2023</span></p>
        <h3>The launch edition</h3>
        <p>32 teams, one track, a borrowed lecture theatre and a printed poster. The problem statement
          sheet went out an hour late, which is exactly why the schedule on this site is versioned.</p>
        <p class="small muted"><strong>Winner:</strong> StudyBuddy - a study-group matcher that later
          became a student society tool.</p>
        <p><a href="gallery.html">View archive photos &rarr;</a></p>
      </article>

      <article class="card">
        <figure class="media">
          <img src="assets/img/past-2.svg" width="700" height="500" alt="CodeStorm 2024 edition artwork">
        </figure>
        <p style="margin-top:1rem"><span class="badge">2024</span></p>
        <h3>The crossover year</h3>
        <p>74 teams and the first all-female winning team, taking the Sustainability track with a
          food-waste tracker that is still deployed in the campus cafeteria.</p>
        <p class="small muted"><strong>Winner:</strong> PlateShare - kitchen-level waste logging with a
          weekly public dashboard.</p>
        <p><a href="gallery.html">View archive photos &rarr;</a></p>
      </article>

      <article class="card">
        <figure class="media">
          <img src="assets/img/past-1.svg" width="700" height="500" alt="CodeStorm 2025 edition artwork">
        </figure>
        <p style="margin-top:1rem"><span class="badge badge--accent">2025</span></p>
        <h3>The 100-team milestone</h3>
        <p>102 teams across four tracks, 212 survey responses and a submission server that nearly
          collapsed at 11:52 on the final morning - hence the second server in 2026.</p>
        <p class="small muted"><strong>Winner:</strong> AccessMap, an indoor navigation aid for
          wheelchair users on campus.</p>
        <p><a href="gallery.html">View archive photos &rarr;</a></p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

